WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:07.269 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hey there everyone just wanted to do a  shorter video for a change i'm still  working on bigger projects such as the  aftermath of the calamity and my  personal skyward sword review but these  will take a while to complete it's a lot  of work and on top of that i'm taking a  two week summer break just so i can you  know enjoy some free time away from the  computer and away from building chicken  coops the chickens are doing fine by the  way today i want to take a quick look at  a topic which has intrigued me ever  since i became aware of it though i must  be clear that although i did find this  on my own without anyone telling me  about it i am definitely not the first  to make this connection for instance one  of my discord mods cuckoo lover recently  made an in-depth video about the  possible symbolism and connections to  spirituality we might see in breath of  the wild too another video i highly  recommend watching if you're interested  in this topic is a video made by  nintendo black crisis about the ancient  cistern which besides talking about the  dungeon itself also presents a lot of  knowledge on buddhist traditions and  symbolism i'll put links to these two  videos in the description so keep in  mind i'm not trying to take credit for  anything i'm just here to present this  finding to those who may have missed it  so you may remember these weird statues  that we found in the breath of the wild  2 trailer prior to finishing skyward  sword myself i referred to these statues  as well as the shapes on this new golem  creature in the trailer of breathtaking  as pine cones or well pinecone things to  be exact but it has since become clear  to me that these are most likely not  pine cones but instead they are lotus  flowers to some this may seem trivial i  mean it's just a decoration right but  the lotus flower symbolism seen here  could actually be a very important clue  as to what we can expect from the sequel  to breath of the wild the significance  of the lotus flower cannot be  understated as it has direct connections  to something that people have been  trying to piece together ever since this  year's e3 namely what are these floating  islands why are they here where did they  come from why have they remained  invisible up until now and what will  their role be in the new game there have  been plenty of ideas about these  floating landmasses ever since we first  saw them some think it's similar to  skyloft where a magic cloud barrier  created by goddess hylia prevents people  from seeing this world above the clouds  even when the sky is clear others think  it might be the sacred realm or that we  didn't see these islands before because  breath of the wild 2 will take place in  a different time period there's no  shortage of speculation here one idea  which i have increasingly become a  supporter of is that this area of the  game is somehow connected to the spirit  realm a place where higher beings like  spirit guardians and perhaps even the  spirits of those who passed on reside  it's been made clear on many occasions  that a place like this exists in the  zelda universe in fact we visited a  location like this in skyward sword here  they are called silent realms and phi  makes it clear that these are the  domains of the spirits a place where the  living are not welcome unless given  special privilege by the gods or goddess  hylia in this case this is also where  the significance of the lotus flower  immediately becomes apparent in buddhism  the lotus among other things represents  purity and enlightenment and in skyward  sword it is used to represent the  spiritual growth link undergoes as well  as a way to justify this collectathon  but that's beside the point whenever  link enters the silent realm an orb will  emerge from his chest which then  manifests into a flower which is very  similar to the spirit orbs in breath of  the wild the spirit vessel as it is  referred to needs to be filled up  completely after which the flower at the  top will close creating a similar shape  to the one we see in the breath of the  wild 2 trailer the reason i initially  didn't make the connection between the  lotus flower and this shape is because  it's missing the plume at the top you  know where the petals come together so  that's why i called it a pinecone  instead but one quick glance at places  like the ancient cistern shows that this  plume doesn't have to be there as we see  plenty of lotus depictions that don't  have this feature either it's clear that  out of all zelda titles skyward sword is  the game which has the closest  connection to breath of the wild in  terms of its motifs symbolism as well as  the overall references placed in the  game like the springs goddess statues  dragon spirits forgotten temple just to  name a few so it's no surprise that the  sequel 2 will continue this trend as it  is still set in the same world as its  predecessor spirits are once again a  common occurrence in breath of the wild  the koroks elemental dragons lord of the  mountain great fairies and horus god  melania are all classified as spirit  beings they are also invisible to most  people with the exception of certain  chosen individuals like link as well as  young children it's implied that this  has something to do with the purity of  one soul in buddhism as well as  shintoism the age at which one loses its  innocence is said to be around 12 years  old after this point all humans become  impure and will need to purify  themselves we see something like this  play out in skyward sword as well zelda  needs to purify herself inside the  springs in order to become a suitable  vessel for the goddess and link needs to  grow his spirit in order to access the  sacred flames as well as make himself  ready to wield the full triforce the  fact that we see lotus depictions within  the sky realm of breath of the wild 2  almost certainly hints that the skies  he's traversing are more than just some  floating islands above the clouds but in  fact closely tied to the world of  spirits so another dimension altogether  which also explains why we don't see the  islands from the surface and as many  have pointed out this is further evident  from the strange portals the dragons use  to make their exit it's amazing to me  that the zelda team implemented details  like these into the game as it really  makes you feel like the story events of  the sequel were planned and purposely  hinted at all along i don't know if this  is the case but if it is props to them  as of right now it's unclear what the  goal of link's trip to the sky realm is  and to me this is very exciting it could  have something to do with the triforce  or at the very least the triforce of  courage since link from breath of the  wild is one of only a few incarnations  of link who as of right now has not  obtained the triforce of courage at any  point in his career as a hero he is  recognized as a true hero by mong mas  koshia as well as zelda herself but the  holy relic has eluded him thus far  obviously this wasn't necessary in  breath of the wild seeing as calamity  ganon wasn't a real entity but a mere  ghost created by malice i mean even the  master sword wasn't crucial to defeating  him which already raised a lot of  suspicion in breath of the wild too  however it seems link and zelda will be  dealing with the source of malice and  the true form of the demon king hence  obtaining the triforce or at the very  least the piece of courage might be the  motivation to travel to the heavenly  realm alternatively it could be that  link has been corrupted by malice with  his body and soul now tainted and impure  from his affliction he may need to  cleanse himself by entering the spirit  realm it could even explain the absence  of the master sword as it may have  rejected him now that he's been  corrupted by evil another option and yep  i'm gonna have to mention the zonai  again they might have something to do  with it their sudden disappearance could  mean that they have all died and passed  on to the afterlife if the zonai who are  described as having been powerful magic  wielders somehow possessed the key or  the knowledge to ganondorf's defeat be  it the triforce of courage or some other  powerful ability this could be the  reason why link has to travel to the  spirit realm as it could be the only way  to obtain this power or knowledge by  gaining an audience with the spirits of  these ancient warriors zelda's  disappearance or even possible death as  dark as that would be could also have  something to do with it it's not like  zelda's spirit hasn't been separated  from her body before you know what that  would totally explain why we hear  zelda's lullaby at the end of the  trailer it is unmistakably her theme but  instead of the usual flute or harp the  theme is played using the same  instrument as the one we hear for the  dragon deities which as stated before  are spirits  [Music]  [Music]  maybe this signifies that zelda's spirit  is trapped in the spirit world or the  underworld as she is seen falling down  so maybe link travels to the spirit  world to somehow free her soul some  might also be pleased to know that  although the champions and king rome  passed on to the afterlife at the end of  breath the wild the possible existence  of a spirit world in breath while 2  could mean that we will see them again  after all maybe not with a very big role  this time around and probably only in  spirit form yet again but still there  are plenty of possibilities and of  course if you have your own ideas don't  hesitate to share them down in the  comments a good discussion is always  welcome who knows what we might find in  this other realm it's been long since  revealed that breath of the wild was  initially supposed to feature a  minish-like race of tiny creatures link  could interact with the minish last seen  in minish cap share a lot of traits with  that of the koroks in that they are  invisible to most people and mostly show  themselves to children alone the realm  of the minish is also said to reside  close to the heavens and we even see a  symbol very similar to that of vati who  is revealed to have been a minish  himself not saying vati will make an  appearance in breath while too though  that would be awesome but it could be  more than just a reference and yet  another clue that ties the sky from  breath to wall 2 to some higher plane of  existence and that's pretty much it for  this one again this was more of a stray  thought than a well-constructed theory  but i gotta give myself a break once in  a while as stated at the beginning  bigger stuff is on the way but it will  take a while before they see the light  of day right now i'm focused on only two  things taking a break and going on a  nice trip and playing metroid dread  which i'm very excited for i also want  to apologize for the lack of streams  lately i've been having some very  annoying technical issues the biggest of  which being my internet shutting down at  random i've contacted my provider about  this and they are looking into it but  apparently it's not just my internet but  the entire block is having this problem  so until this is resolved i won't be  able to stream properly so i hope you  can bear with me as always thank you so  much for watching the support the kind  words and the comments the whole thing i  cannot stress enough how much this all  means to me you guys make my day time  and time again and i'm humbled that i  can do this stuff for a living your  likes comments feedback and all that  good jazz not only motivates me but also  teaches me all sorts of things i didn't  know and that is worth so much to me a  special shout out goes to my patreons  and members as always as well as my  discord and streaming mods you guys are  the best and i'm continuously amazed by  your support your hard work your  feedback just everything you do also  please give a warm welcome to jennifer  butler gamesmiths and roseret17 for  joining my crew as well as a special  thanks to barky doggo who has been  extremely generous with extra donations  over the past months also keep an eye  out for another special thanks which i  will probably film in person someone  sent me an amazing gift and i want to  highlight it but so far i just haven't  had the time for it so banoon if you are  listening i will cover it soon again  thank you so much to each and every one  of you and that is all for now i hope to  see you in the next video this is dawn  signing off and have a good one  [Music]  you

